CORRECTION to ZAXON-WAS-ASKED-FOR-AS-A-WORKI-20260804-094335.idea, same day: ZAXON EXISTS AND IS RUNNING. That idea claimed it was unbuilt. Wrong. I searched ~/Documents/Projects, GitHub and PATH ON MANDARK, and zaxon is on none of those because it does not run on mandark: it runs as user zaxon in a SEPARATE WSL distribution called hermes on dexter -- a third userland no ecosystem document mentions. hermes-gateway.service ('Hermes Agent Gateway - Messaging Platform Integration') is active, alongside a whisper.cpp STT server. It exposes an MCP server over streamable-http with exactly two tools, ask_zach and check_zach_reply, relaying to Zach's WhatsApp. Verified working end to end 2026-08-04: sent ticket 92ef550c from mandark over the tailnet. Reachability probed per host and written up in realisateur/ZAXON.md (also copied to /srv/dog/ZAXON.md for the corpus agent): mandark reaches it at http://100.107.253.56:8643/mcp; MONKEY reaches it at http://10.0.2.2:8643/mcp via the VirtualBox NAT gateway, which is the non-obvious one and means a project account inside the VM can ask Zach a question even though it is not on the tailnet; monkey CANNOT use the tailscale address. No auth on the port. THE LESSON, which is the durable part: 'I looked and found nothing' is only as strong as the set of places looked at. I reported ABSENCE with confidence after searching one host, which is precisely the BLIND-reported-as-OK failure this ecosystem built silence-audit to catch, committed by the agent that maintains it.
